From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Notice files: the nearest one above a module that has none

The image's legal notices (/system/etc/NOTICE.html.gz, Settings > About >
Legal information) list a module only if its own directory holds a NOTICE
file. Most modules sit below the directory that does, the project's: in the
PW3 image (Test V38) SurfaceFlinger, installd, the HIDL services, the
SwiftShader libraries and every PW3 module were missing, 878 installed files
in all.

A module without a NOTICE of its own now takes the nearest NOTICE in a
directory above it, else the nearest licence file: SwiftShader has only a
LICENSE.txt, libjpeg-turbo a LICENSE.md (its IJG terms ask for a notice with
every binary), VIXL a LICENCE, strace a COPYING. Only modules installed on
the device are looked up so: the notices are for what the device carries. A
module with a licence of its own below such a project has to name it, as
before (LOCAL_NOTICE_FILE or its own NOTICE). Projects with no licence file
anywhere above a module (system/vold, frameworks/rs and a few others of
AOSP's own, all Apache-2.0) stay unlisted, as in AOSP.

--- a/core/notice_files.mk
+++ b/core/notice_files.mk
@@ -8,6 +8,16 @@
 else
 notice_file:=$(strip $(wildcard $(LOCAL_PATH)/NOTICE))
 endif
+# An installed module without one of its own: the project's, the nearest
+# above the module.
+ifdef LOCAL_INSTALLED_MODULE
+ifeq ($(notice_file),)
+notice_file:=$(firstword $(call find-parent-file,$(LOCAL_PATH),NOTICE))
+endif
+ifeq ($(notice_file),)
+notice_file:=$(firstword $(call find-parent-file,$(LOCAL_PATH),LICENSE LICENSE.txt LICENSE.md LICENCE COPYING))
+endif
+endif
 
 ifeq ($(LOCAL_MODULE_CLASS),GYP)
   # We ignore NOTICE files for modules of type GYP.
